  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Three clear drops sealed in a bead of glass, which do not run together however the bead is turned. Flies that land on the bead do not get up again.</p><p><strong>Coat a Weapon.</strong> As a Bonus Action, you coat one weapon or one piece of ammunition; the poison stays potent for 1 hour and is used up by the first hit. The creature hit makes a [[/save ability=con dc=22 format=long]], taking [[/damage 20d6 type=poison]] damage on a failed save or half as much on a success. This damage ignores Resistance and treats Immunity to Poison damage as Resistance. On a failed save the creature also cannot regain Hit Points for 1 minute.</p><p><strong>It Cannot Be Unmade.</strong> A wound from these tears never closes cleanly. The scar stays cold for the rest of the creature's existence and aches when the poisoner is near, in whatever form either of them then wears. Things that cannot die have been known to bargain to avoid it.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
